From 3bf4a223f7765a05597849691eb76da34d7e5cc8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: meanaverage <18336095+meanaverage@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 11:26:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): audio playback (RDPSND) through an `audioPlayback`
 callback

The web client had no audio output. An RDPSND client backend (16-bit PCM
at 48, 44.1 and 22.05 kHz) now forwards what the server sends to the
session loop, which hands it to the JavaScript callback given with the new
`audioPlayback(callback)` extension: `{ type: 'wave', sampleRate,
channels, data }`, `{ type: 'volume', left, right }` and
`{ type: 'close' }`. With a callback, audio playback is enabled in the
client info; without one, nothing changes.

Windows servers only start playback once RDPDR is up as well (FreeRDP
enables device redirection along with audio for the same reason), so a
device-less RDPDR is attached when no printer is.
